Imagine your school has a big meeting where grown-ups decide new rules for everyone. In China, there is a big meeting like that for the whole country. It’s called the **National People Congress**.

It’s a group of grown-ups who help make the rules for China. They meet in **Beijing**, which is like China’s capital city. They talk and vote about new laws — rules about things like schools, cars, money, and how the country should work. They also help choose China’s most important leaders.

So, the National People Congress is like **China’s big rule-making and leader-choosing team**. It’s a bit like Parliament in London, but for China. [end of text]


